{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 995016,
  "courseSlug": "vuejs-2-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Vue - The Complete Guide (incl. Router & Composition API)",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "21463566",
      "title": "Provide + Inject To The Rescue",
      "lectureOrder": 105,
      "videoOrder": 89,
      "sourceHash": "0d0a2158f77ab9cc47665653af7526849bd9fc2b96413623c11c121fc7363c4c",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.12,
          "end": 4.54,
          "en": "So how does Vue help us solve",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.54,
          "end": 6.79,
          "en": "such pass-through problems?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.79,
          "end": 9.43,
          "en": "First of all, it's really important to understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.43,
          "end": 12.71,
          "en": "that this is not necessarily a problem, and not bad.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.71,
          "end": 15.64,
          "en": "You can do it the way we're doing it here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.64,
          "end": 19.04,
          "en": "but to save writing that extra code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.04,
          "end": 22.89,
          "en": "you can also get rid of, let's say the props here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.89,
          "end": 24.17,
          "en": "let's start with topics.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.17,
          "end": 25.83,
          "en": "You can't get rid of that here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.83,
          "end": 28.61,
          "en": "get rid of it here, on KnowledgeGrid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.61,
          "end": 32.26,
          "en": "And for the moment, just keep that emitted event,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.26,
          "end": 35.27,
          "en": "and then pass the topics to KnowledgeGrid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.27,
          "end": 36.41,
          "en": "in a different way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 36.41,
          "end": 38.59,
          "en": "Because we need to topic steer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 38.59,
          "end": 42.74,
          "en": "and we definitely, also need to manage them in App.vue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 42.74,
          "end": 46.5,
          "en": "Since App.vue, is the place where active element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 46.5,
          "end": 49.4,
          "en": "which needs to know about the topics, and KnowledgeBase,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 49.4,
          "end": 53.51,
          "en": "and therefor, ultimately KnowledgeGrid are connected.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 53.51,
          "end": 56.6,
          "en": "So how can we pass the topics to KnowledgeGrid,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 56.6,
          "end": 58.12,
          "en": "which needs to topics,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 58.12,
          "end": 60.763,
          "en": "if we don't want to pass them through KnowledgeBase?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 61.95,
          "end": 63.93,
          "en": "Well, first of all, let's remove them here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 63.93,
          "end": 67.65,
          "en": "and let's explore another feature Vue offers us,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 67.65,
          "end": 71.56,
          "en": "and that is, provide and inject,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 71.56,
          "end": 74.9,
          "en": "a pattern you can use to provide data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 74.9,
          "end": 77.5,
          "en": "in one place and inject it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 77.5,
          "end": 81,
          "en": "which means use it, in another place.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 81,
          "end": 83.41,
          "en": "Now here in App.vue, we could, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 83.41,
          "end": 86.06,
          "en": "provide our topics here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 86.06,
          "end": 88.68,
          "en": "We do this by adding a provide option",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 88.68,
          "end": 92.7,
          "en": "to our conflict object, anywhere in the conflict object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 92.7,
          "end": 96.2,
          "en": "Here I'm adding it between data and methods.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 96.2,
          "end": 99.45,
          "en": "And provide can hold an object then,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 99.45,
          "end": 103.6,
          "en": "in which you, for example, provide your topics.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 103.6,
          "end": 108.3,
          "en": "So here, I could then grab this topics array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 108.3,
          "end": 110.59,
          "en": "and provide it down there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 110.59,
          "end": 113.083,
          "en": "So now I'm providing this topics array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 114.61,
          "end": 115.85,
          "en": "Now this is step one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 115.85,
          "end": 118.2,
          "en": "Now we're providing this data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 118.2,
          "end": 121.98,
          "en": "and that uses an internal mechanism built into Vue,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 121.98,
          "end": 125.2,
          "en": "but providing is only half of the story.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 125.2,
          "end": 128.84,
          "en": "We also need to listen to that provided data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 128.84,
          "end": 131.94,
          "en": "We need to use that provided data somewhere,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 131.94,
          "end": 134,
          "en": "and that in our case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 134,
          "end": 135.97,
          "en": "which take place in the KnowledgeGrid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 135.97,
          "end": 139.01,
          "en": "because that is where we need the topics.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 139.01,
          "end": 140.64,
          "en": "For that here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 140.64,
          "end": 144.35,
          "en": "rather than expecting to get topics as props,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 144.35,
          "end": 148.25,
          "en": "we add another option, the inject option.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 148.25,
          "end": 150.84,
          "en": "Which works together with provide.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 150.84,
          "end": 155.39,
          "en": "Inject, basically works like props, you provide an array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 155.39,
          "end": 159.48,
          "en": "and now you reference all the provided data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 159.48,
          "end": 162.13,
          "en": "you wanna use in this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 162.13,
          "end": 164.43,
          "en": "So at the moment, there's just one piece of data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 164.43,
          "end": 167.82999999999998,
          "en": "we are providing, and that would be topics.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 167.82999999999998,
          "end": 172.06,
          "en": "We're providing that in App.vue, under the key topics here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 172.06,
          "end": 177.06,
          "en": "So we can use that key, and inject here in KnowledgeGrid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 180.98,
          "end": 182.64,
          "en": "And here's one important note,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 182.64,
          "end": 185.96,
          "en": "you can only inject what has been provided",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 185.96,
          "end": 188.33,
          "en": "on a higher-up level.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 188.33,
          "end": 190.97,
          "en": "Which basically means, in a parent component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 190.97,
          "end": 193.843,
          "en": "or an ancestor component of KnowledgeGrid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 194.81,
          "end": 197.29,
          "en": "So we can inject topics here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 197.29,
          "end": 199.8,
          "en": "because it is provided in App vue,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 199.8,
          "end": 204.12,
          "en": "and App vue, ultimately is above KnowledgeGrid, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 204.12,
          "end": 206.52,
          "en": "App vue is a parent to KnowledgeBase,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 206.52,
          "end": 209.14,
          "en": "and KnowledgeBase is a parent KnowledgeGrid,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 209.14,
          "end": 213.11,
          "en": "and therefore KnowledgeGrid also is below App.vue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 213.11,
          "end": 216.623,
          "en": "If we, for example, provided something in ActiveElement,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 217.61,
          "end": 220.98,
          "en": "we could not inject it in KnowledgeGrid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 220.98,
          "end": 221.813,
          "en": "Why?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 221.813,
          "end": 225.21,
          "en": "Because ActiveElement is a neighbor of Knowledgebase,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 225.21,
          "end": 228.623,
          "en": "and KnowledgeBase den contains KnowledgeGrid,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 229.474,
          "end": 232.29,
          "en": "and therefore, ultimately, ActiveElement is a neighbor",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 232.29,
          "end": 233.323,
          "en": "to KnowledgeGrid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 234.38,
          "end": 235.231,
          "en": "And this will not work, provide, and inject",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 235.231,
          "end": 240.03,
          "en": "needs this, parent-child relation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 240.03,
          "end": 243.62,
          "en": "So you can't provide and inject between neighbors,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 243.62,
          "end": 247.18,
          "en": "but here it will work because we are providing an App.vue,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 247.18,
          "end": 250.58,
          "en": "and that is an ancestor of KnowledgeGrid,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 250.58,
          "end": 252.35,
          "en": "So it is above KnowledgeGrid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 252.35,
          "end": 254.95,
          "en": "And there for, now if you save this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 254.95,
          "end": 258.47,
          "en": "you will see that everything still works as before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 258.47,
          "end": 262.73,
          "en": "but now data is ending up differently in KnowledgeGrid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 262.73,
          "end": 266.96,
          "en": "And we're avoiding this passing-through of topics",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 266.96,
          "end": 271.32,
          "en": "in KnowledgeBase, which is definitely an improvement here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 271.32,
          "end": 273.38,
          "en": "However, there is a problem,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 273.38,
          "end": 277.75,
          "en": "we're now basically, creating this array twice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 277.75,
          "end": 281.15,
          "en": "We have it here, in App.vue in our data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 281.15,
          "end": 284.6,
          "en": "and we then have it again, in the provide object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 284.6,
          "end": 288.52,
          "en": "This works in this case, but it is code duplication.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 288.52,
          "end": 292.17,
          "en": "And if we had any logic in this app to change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 292.17,
          "end": 294.57,
          "en": "this data stored array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 294.57,
          "end": 298.3,
          "en": "this change would not be reflected in the provided data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 298.3,
          "end": 300.21,
          "en": "because that's a brand new array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 300.21,
          "end": 303.9,
          "en": "It's a brand new object in memory there for.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 303.9,
          "end": 307.8,
          "en": "So if we ever changed his original array here in data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 307.8,
          "end": 311.56,
          "en": "such changes would not be passed on to components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 311.56,
          "end": 313.913,
          "en": "that rely on the provided topics.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 315.18,
          "end": 317.64,
          "en": "Therefore, it would be nicer if we could provide",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 317.64,
          "end": 322.64,
          "en": "our data here, so that eventually changes are picked up.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 322.75,
          "end": 325.2,
          "en": "And it turns out, we can do that for that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 325.2,
          "end": 329.85,
          "en": "for that we need to change the way we use provide though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 329.85,
          "end": 332.38,
          "en": "Instead of setting it equal to an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 332.38,
          "end": 334.32,
          "en": "with the provided data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 334.32,
          "end": 337.12,
          "en": "we now convert provide to a method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 337.12,
          "end": 340.77,
          "en": "so now to provide option holds a function in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 340.77,
          "end": 343.99,
          "en": "And in there we return our provided object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 343.99,
          "end": 347.40999999999997,
          "en": "so it now basically, works a little bit like data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 347.40999999999997,
          "end": 351.13,
          "en": "And then here, we can still set up any keys of our choice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 351.13,
          "end": 353.11,
          "en": "so I will stick to topics here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 353.11,
          "end": 356.124,
          "en": "but now we can use the this keyword to reach out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 356.124,
          "end": 359.26,
          "en": "to our instant specific data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 359.26,
          "end": 361.01,
          "en": "So with these topics,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 361.01,
          "end": 365.33,
          "en": "I now reach out to topics which we manage in our data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 365.33,
          "end": 369.15,
          "en": "And I'm using this, to provide it under a topics key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 369.15,
          "end": 371.713,
          "en": "to any potential child components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 372.61,
          "end": 374.79,
          "en": "Of course, this key you're using here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 374.79,
          "end": 377.71,
          "en": "doesn't have to be the same one you're using in data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 377.71,
          "end": 380.253,
          "en": "It is in this case, but it doesn't have to be.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 381.44,
          "end": 383.74,
          "en": "If I now save is, it still works,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 383.74,
          "end": 388.16,
          "en": "but now we are working on one and the same object in memory.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 388.16,
          "end": 392.74,
          "en": "Now let's simulate that topics changes here in our data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 392.74,
          "end": 395.49,
          "en": "to verify whether this is really works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 395.49,
          "end": 400.49,
          "en": "For this, I'm going to add the mounted lifecycle hook here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 403.52,
          "end": 407.42,
          "en": "and in there, I'll set a timer to let's say three seconds.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 407.42,
          "end": 411.21,
          "en": "And after those three seconds, in this array function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 411.21,
          "end": 412.46,
          "en": "which is just a different way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 412.46,
          "end": 415.04,
          "en": "of defining a function JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 415.04,
          "end": 419.21,
          "en": "I will reach out to this topics and push a new topic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 419.21,
          "end": 420.85,
          "en": "to the array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 420.85,
          "end": 424.9,
          "en": "That topic will have an id of events let's say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 424.9,
          "end": 429.9,
